  "issue_number": 620,
  "issue_title": "provider(optional_ai_provider): expose model selection instead of hardcoding model=\"default\"",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nThe optional OpenAI-compatible provider path currently provides no way to configure the outbound model name and always serializes generic requests with `\"model\":\"default\"`.\n\nThat leaves the newly merged optional-provider path only partially parameterized: provider selection is config-driven, but provider model selection is not.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWhen `[optional_ai_provider].enabled = true`, GenieClaw should either:\n\n- let the operator configure the model id used for outbound OpenAI-compatible chat requests, or\n- fail loudly when the optional provider path is enabled without a usable model id.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nGeneric OpenAI-compatible requests are serialized with a hardcoded model name:\n\n- `crates/genie-core/src/llm/openai_compat.rs`\n  - `RequestProfile::Generic => \"default\"`\n  - `serialize_body()` writes that value into the outbound `ChatRequest`\n\nThere is already a unit test asserting this behavior:\n\n- `generic_request_profile_keeps_full_default_body`\n- `assert_eq!(json[\"model\"], \"default\")`\n\nAt the same time, `[optional_ai_provider]` has no model field in config or docs.\n\n## Why this is a problem\n\nMany OpenAI-compatible backends require a real model id and do not accept a placeholder such as `\"default\"`.\n\nThat means the optional provider path can:\n\n1. validate successfully,\n2. boot successfully, and then\n3. still emit unusable requests because the model is not parameterized.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Configure an optional provider:\n\n```toml\n[optional_ai_provider]\nenabled = true\nprovider = \"open_ai_compatible\"\nauth_mode = \"api_key\"\nbase_url = \"http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1\"\napi_key_env = \"PROVIDER_KEY\"\ncontext_window_tokens = 4096\nallow_remote_base_url = false\n```\n\n2. Point `base_url` at a local mock OpenAI-compatible server that records request bodies.\n3. Build the client through `LlmClient::from_config()`.\n4. Send a chat request.\n5. Observe the outgoing JSON contains:\n\n```json\n{\"model\":\"default\", ...}\n```\n\n## Root cause hypothesis\n\nThe generic OpenAI-compatible request profile hardcodes the model string, and `[optional_ai_provider]` exposes no matching model field, so the provider path is selectable but not fully parameterizable.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n- Add a model field under `[optional_ai_provider]`\n- Thread it through `LlmClient::from_config()` into the generic OpenAI-compatible request profile\n- Fail loudly when the optional provider path is enabled without a usable model id\n- Add a request-capture test that verifies the configured model is emitted\n\n## Impact\n\n- Optional provider setup appears valid while still sending unusable requests\n- Blocks real use of many OpenAI-compatible endpoints\n- Leaves the provider work from #568 / #595 incomplete on the \u201cparameterize the provider\u201d requirement\n\n## References\n\n- #568\n- #595\n- `crates/genie-common/src/config.rs`\n- `crates/genie-core/src/llm/mod.rs`\n- `crates/genie-core/src/llm/openai_compat.rs`\n- `doc/configuration.md`\n",
